        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12357401/comment/12454854",
          "id": "12454854",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=oglueck",
            "name": "oglueck",
            "key": "oglueck",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Ortwin Glueck",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Zurich"
          },
          "body": "Proposed patch incl. test cases.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=oglueck",
            "name": "oglueck",
            "key": "oglueck",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Ortwin Glueck",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Zurich"
          },
          "created": "2006-12-01T09:37:58.000+0000",
          "updated": "2006-12-01T09:37:58.000+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12357401/comment/12454858",
          "id": "12454858",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=olegk",
            "name": "olegk",
            "key": "olegk",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Oleg Kalnichevski",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "body": "Odi,\n\nIn those cases when the content length is not known (because chunk or identity transfer encoding is being used, for insyance) I think it would be more efficient to use  ByteArrayOutputStream instead of pre-allocating the maxLen of bytes. Consider the situation where maxLen is rather largish (say several MB) and chunk coded-content is just a couple of KB.\n\nOleg",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=olegk",
            "name": "olegk",
            "key": "olegk",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Oleg Kalnichevski",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "created": "2006-12-01T09:57:14.000+0000",
          "updated": "2006-12-01T09:57:14.000+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12357401/comment/12454864",
          "id": "12454864",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=oglueck",
            "name": "oglueck",
            "key": "oglueck",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Ortwin Glueck",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Zurich"
          },
          "body": "True. What about the initial size of the ByteArrayOutputStream? By default it's 32 bytes. This means lots of copying and object allocations when the content is large. I guess this makes the method unsuitable for high-performance / low-footprint applications. But those applications are better off using getResponseBodyAsStream() anyway. It's just a convenience method after all.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=oglueck",
            "name": "oglueck",
            "key": "oglueck",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Ortwin Glueck",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Zurich"
          },
          "created": "2006-12-01T10:18:27.000+0000",
          "updated": "2006-12-01T10:18:27.000+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12357401/comment/12454870",
          "id": "12454870",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=olegk",
            "name": "olegk",
            "key": "olegk",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Oleg Kalnichevski",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "body": "We should apply the same logic as in #getResponseBody method at the very least for the consistency sake:\n\nByteArrayOutputStream outstream = new ByteArrayOutputStream(\n  contentLength > 0 ? (int) contentLength : DEFAULT_INITIAL_BUFFER_SIZE);\n\nOtherwise +1 to commit\n\nOleg",
          "updateAuthor": {
